ation" (cons (quoted (cons "    (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §9.3 “An exact decoded machine and a structural compiler theorem”, " (cons "Loading, native substitution, and export" (cons "). Today `#jit` binds x86 bytes with no relation, which breaks this rule." nil)))) (cons "  - The x86 translator (`src/lang.c`'s native path, `lib/x86.cub`, `lib/machine.cub`, `lib/elf.cub`'s" (cons "    pasted machine code, `lib/compile/`) is superseded." (cons (quoted (cons "- **The laws of the primitives,** each a theorem or a named assumption (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…, §8.5 “Machine representations and memory laws”, " (cons "Exact scalar types" (cons ")." nil)))) (cons "- **Deriving,** as a typed term." (cons "- **Terms of any depth.**" (cons "" (cons "**Dimensions.** This is answered by the standard semantics; it was never a question for Avik." (cons "- In CCHM a term in Γ; Ψ; φ means a family natural in the stage: an element of A at every Ψ′ with a" (cons "  substitution Ψ′ → Ψ satisfying φ, commuting with every further substitution." (cons "- A dimension's value at a stage is an element of the free De Morgan algebra on that stage's names," (cons "  and the substitutions are maps of that algebra. This is the cubical-set model." (cons "- So the number of dimensions varies only in the quantification over stages. A semantic action of" (cons "  interval expressions, defined on syntax, must be shown once to respect the algebra's equations." (cons "  That is the well-definedness of the cube category's action, not a cost of the encoding." (cons "- `lib/nbe.cub` is that model inside the host:" (cons "  - stages are host cubes (`Cube n`);" (cons "  - interval expressions are data (`IEx`, `DNF`);" (cons "  - substitutions are `Sub` and `cmap-d`." (cons "- Its steps map onto the obligations:" (cons "  - F2a–F2c are the well-definedness (every De Morgan law, with no 2-cell);" (cons "  - F2d is the normalize